     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Making adverbs",
     "md": "Many adverbs end in **-ly**: slow → slowly, quick → quickly, loud → loudly, kind → kindly. Some are special: fast, hard, well."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "- *Run quick* is wrong; say *run quickly*.\n- Good is an adjective; well is an adverb: *She sings well*.\n- Adverbs tell about verbs; adjectives tell about nouns."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Find the adverb: The baby sleeps quietly.",
     "steps": [
      "Sleeps is the verb.",
      "Quietly tells how: it is the adverb."
     ],
     "answer": "quietly",
